==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 31.33 seconds<sup>940f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Dark Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Dark Cat]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is almost mandatory here, as without him the Angelic Gories will push extremely hard and wipe out your backline attackers. Due to Sunfish Jones' presence, it is important to remember to not bring any knockback units (with the exception of [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], who you should only send out if there are no other attackers on the field.)

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Mandatory to prevent the Angelic Gories from pushing too hard, he can act as a solo meatshield here provided you bring a [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|medium research combo]] or [[Biohazard (Combo)|2 small]] [[Bony Bone (Combo)|research combos]].
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]: Your main source of damage for this stage. Bahamut's high range and high damage will be extremely helpful in chipping down Li'l Dark. If you have his True Form [[Talents|Talented]], however, he heavily cripples Li'l Dark and can kill it in 2-3 cycles. Using [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] is recommended.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Delivery Cat]]: Helpful unit in disposing of the Angelic Gory waves, with his Massive Damage vs. Angels, he can make quick work of each Angelic Gory wave. The True Form is recommended for even higher power, though its stages are more difficult comparatively.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: If you're doing this stage later on, this unit can deal high midrange DPS towards the Angels in this stage. Do note it cannot outrange Li'l Dark.
*[[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]: A stackable long range unit who helps chip down Li'l Dark and can also kill the peons in this stage. '''Do not''' use Ururun when you have a stack of them on the field, as she will knockback the boss into the range of Sunfish Jones and get your stack evaporated. You should have enough money to buy him when his cooldown ends, just like Ramen Cat, so spam him whenever you are able to.

